  "body": "From the merge-order analysis of 2026-11-22. AGENTS.md, \"Heavy lanes at review\" (#2568): the author runs `cargo xtask gate heavy` on the final head of each PR whose diff reaches a heavy lane. One run of the motion and app lanes takes 60 to 70 minutes, and only one heavy build can run at a time on a machine. For a wave of 9 PRs that reach the lanes, this is about 12 hours.\n\n## Proposal (the maintainer decides; this changes AGENTS.md)\nA wave of PRs that the planner puts in one group can use ONE heavy run on the trial tree of the wave: the current `main` with each PR of the wave merged. The run covers each PR, because the tree contains each diff. The result is recorded on each PR of the wave (the tree hash, the lanes, the counts). If the run is red, the red step is attributed to a PR, that PR leaves the wave, and the run starts again for the rest.\n\nRules that stay:\n- \"Not run\" is never a pass.\n- A PR that merges alone keeps the rule of today.\n- The release tier at the cut stays the final check.\n\n## Necessary work\n1. A decision entry in `docs/decisions/` with the maintainer's answer.\n2. The text of AGENTS.md (\"Heavy lanes at review\") and of the `gate`, `merge-ready` and `review-prs` skills.\n3. `cargo xtask gate heavy` accepts a trial tree and prints the list of the PR heads that it covers.\n\nThe PR has `Process change: yes`.\n",
